<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>{{template "site-head" .}}</head>
<body hc-data="site()" id="top">
  {{template "site-nav" .}}
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-enter>A full-stack HTMX framework for Go</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title" data-enter>Stay close<br>to the <em>web.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-description" data-enter>Build expressive applications with Go and HTML.<br>Keep the moving parts that matter.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions" data-enter><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs">Start building <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#playground">Take it for a spin <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art">
        <div class="sculpture" id="sculpture" role="img" aria-label="A full-width torus network of connected nodes with pulses travelling between them">
          <picture>
            <source media="(max-width: 767px)" srcset="/static/img/network-mobile.webp">
            <img class="sculpture-poster" src="/static/img/network.webp" alt="" width="1440" height="810" fetchpriority="high">
          </picture>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="art-controls"><span>Browser → Go → HTML</span><button class="motion-control" hc-on:click="toggleMotion()" hc-bind:aria-pressed="paused" aria-pressed="false" hc-text="paused ? 'Play motion' : 'Pause motion'">Pause motion</button></div>
      <div class="hero-foot"><span>Built with HyperChi. Including this page.</span><span>chi routing <span class="separator">/</span> htmx 4 <span class="separator">/</span> Go templates</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="manifesto section-space" aria-labelledby="manifesto-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">A shorter path from idea to interface</p>
      <h2 id="manifesto-title" data-reveal>The web already<br>has <span class="accent">good bones.</span></h2>
      <div class="manifesto-bottom"><p>URLs. Forms. Requests. HTML.<br>HyperChi brings them together with Go, then gives you the tools to make them feel alive.</p><p>Render on the server. Stream an update. Add a little local state. Spend your attention on what you’re building.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/routing">Meet the framework ↗</a></div>
      <div class="flow-type" aria-hidden="true"><span>request</span><span class="flow-arrow">↗</span><span class="flow-go">Go</span><span class="flow-arrow">↘</span><span>response</span></div>
    </section>

    <section id="playground" class="playground section-space" aria-labelledby="playground-title">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">The live playground</p><h2 id="playground-title">Less explaining.<br><span class="accent">More trying.</span></h2><p>These controls talk to a real Go server.<br>Make a request. Watch the web do its thing.</p></div>
      <noscript><p class="docs-note">Interactive demos need JavaScript. You can still read the <a href="/docs">documentation</a> and explore the source.</p></noscript>
      <div id="flow" class="request-workbench">
        <div class="workbench-code"><div class="pane-heading"><span>index.html</span><span>HTML →</span></div><pre><code><span class="syntax-muted">&lt;!-- A little HTML goes a long way. --&gt;</span>
&lt;<span class="syntax-accent">button</span>
  <span class="syntax-key">hx-get</span>=<span class="syntax-string">"/demo/echo"</span>
  <span class="syntax-key">hx-target</span>=<span class="syntax-string">"#response"</span>&gt;
  Send a request
&lt;/<span class="syntax-accent">button</span>&gt;

&lt;<span class="syntax-accent">div</span> id=<span class="syntax-string">"response"</span>&gt;&lt;/<span class="syntax-accent">div</span>&gt;</code></pre><a href="/docs/routing" class="text-link">Understand the round trip ↗</a></div>
        <div class="workbench-result"><div class="pane-heading"><span>Your browser</span><span>← HTML</span></div><div class="result-stage"><span class="request-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div id="echo-out" aria-live="polite"><p class="muted">Your next request starts here.</p></div><div class="button-row"><button id="send-request" class="btn btn-primary" hx-get="/demo/echo" hx-target="#echo-out" hx-disabled-elt="this">Send a request ↗</button><button class="btn btn-ghost" hx-get="/demo/echo?format=json" hx-target="#echo-out" hx-disabled-elt="this">Try JSON</button></div></div></div>
      </div>
      <div id="proof" class="live-strip"><span class="live-caption">This server,<br>right now.</span><div class="strip" data-stream="/sse?channels=metrics" hx-swap="innerHTML"><div class="metric"><div class="val mono">…</div><div class="lab">requests / sec</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="val mono">…</div><div class="lab">requests total</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="val mono">…</div><div class="lab">uptime</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="val mono">connecting</div><div class="lab">live via SSE</div></div></div></div>

      <div class="experiments">
        <details class="experiment" id="realtime"><summary><span class="experiment-type">WebSockets</span><span class="experiment-title">A room with everyone in it.</span><span class="expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="experiment-body"><div><h3>Say something. See it everywhere.</h3><p>Open another tab and send a message. HyperChi broadcasts it to every browser in the room.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/realtime">Explore realtime ↗</a></div><div hx-ws:connect="/ws?rooms=activity"><div id="activity-log" class="feed" aria-live="polite"><div class="feed-item"><span class="tag">room</span><div class="muted">Connected to the conversation.</div></div></div><form class="message-form" hx-post="/activity/send" hx-swap="none"><label class="sr-only" for="message">Message to the room</label><input id="message" name="message" placeholder="Say hello to another tab…" required maxlength="140"><button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Send ↗</button></form></div></div></details>
        <details class="experiment" id="changelog"><summary><span class="experiment-type">Search + scroll</span><span class="experiment-title">Find it as you type.</span><span class="expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="experiment-body"><div><h3>A small search. A useful pattern.</h3><p>A server-rendered changelog with debounced live search and infinite scrolling.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/regiellis/hyperchi/tree/main/hyperchi/patterns">Read the pattern source ↗</a></div><div><label class="sr-only" for="search">Search the changelog</label><input id="search" name="q" placeholder="Search the changelog…" autocomplete="off" hx-get="/patterns/search" hx-trigger="input changed delay:300ms, search" hx-target="#search-results"><div id="search-results" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="changelog-list" class="feed changelog-list" hx-get="/patterns/changelog?page=1" hx-trigger="load" hx-swap="innerHTML"></div></div></div></details>
        <details class="experiment" id="upload"><summary><span class="experiment-type">File validation</span><span class="experiment-title">Give your uploads a gatekeeper.</span><span class="expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="experiment-body"><div><h3>Check before you accept.</h3><p>Validate a PNG, JPG, WebP, text file, or PDF up to 2 MB. This demo checks your file without storing it.</p></div><div><form hx-post="/upload" hx-target="#upload-out" hx-encoding="multipart/form-data" class="stack"><label class="dropzone">Choose a file to validate<input type="file" name="file" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Validate file ↗</button></form><div id="upload-out" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></details>
        <details class="experiment" id="waitlist"><summary><span class="experiment-type">Forms + autosave</span><span class="experiment-title">One step at a time.</span><span class="expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="experiment-body"><div><h3>Keep the logic on the server.</h3><p>A three-step form with server validation and draft autosaving. Try an invalid email to see the error state.</p></div><div class="panel wizard"><div id="wizard" hx-get="/waitlist?step=1" hx-trigger="load" hx-swap="innerHTML"></div></div></div></details>
      </div>
      <p id="request-error" class="request-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
    </section>

    <section id="matrix" class="capabilities section-space" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title"><div><h2 id="capabilities-title" data-reveal>A small surface.<br>A lot underneath.</h2><p>Bring your HTML. Keep your Go.<br>Reach for the rest when you need it.</p></div><div class="capability-links"><a href="/docs/routing"><span>Routes & responses</span><span>chi + htmx ↗</span></a><a href="/docs/templates"><span>Templates & composition</span><span>Go templates ↗</span></a><a href="/docs/realtime"><span>Live connections</span><span>SSE + WebSockets ↗</span></a><a href="/docs/directives"><span>A little local state</span><span>hc-* directives ↗</span></a></div></section>

    <section id="handout" class="start-section section-space"><p class="eyebrow">Make something of your own</p><h2 data-reveal>Your next idea.<br><span class="accent">A little closer.</span></h2><div class="start-bottom"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs">Build your first page ↗</a><div class="install-command"><code>go get github.com/regiellis/hyperchi</code><button hc-on:click="copyInstall()" hc-text="copyLabel" aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button></div></div><p class="copy-status sr-only" aria-live="polite" hc-text="copyStatus"></p></section>
  </main>
  {{template "site-footer" .}}
  {{template "site-scripts" .}}
  <script src="/hyperchi/js/hx-sse.js"></script>
  <script src="/hyperchi/js/hx-ws.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
